Changes made to CxxIME (2026-10):
- Laya context reranking: a Laya decision model (fine-tuned, then distilled into
  mmBERT-small; ONNX Runtime, CPU or DirectML) picks the
  first candidate for pinyin homophones and English completions from the preceding text;
  the pick is marked with a sparkle in the candidate window
  (engine/src/laya_rerank.cc, engine/src/laya/, ui/src/sparkle.h).
- A word n-gram next to that choice (engine/src/laya/ngram.h): Youmo IME's pinyin language
  model (LGPL-2.1-or-later, based on libime's) with science text mixed in, in ngram/zh.ngram,
  distributed under LGPL-2.1-or-later as its base.
- English word list and English word mode with completion, digit selection and case
  matching; exact English words offered in Chinese mode
  (engine/src/english_lexicon.cc, engine/src/engine.cc).
- Three input modes (Chinese / English words / English letters) with a configurable
  English style shortcut (settings, server session state).
- Removed the floating status window; the right-click menu of the taskbar input indicator
  switches the input states (tsf/src/language_bar.cpp, shared/include/cxxime/ime_menu.h).
- Relicensed the combined work under GPL-3.0-only.
- The models trained by 知意输入法 are distributed under GPL-3.0-only as well, except
  Zhiyi 1.4V2-Long-L12 (the Laya recommendation model in models/laya/ since 1.5.12, release
  model-zhen-long-l12) and the offline translation model v3, whose weights are licensed under
  the Apache License, Version 2.0 (data/licenses/Apache-2.0.txt) since 2026-10-20.
- Renamed to 知意输入法 / Zhiyi IME with new text service and UI GUIDs, pipe, mutex,
  window class, registry, file and data directory names, and new icons.
- Fixed an out-of-bounds read in SpellingsIndex::load and the node count written by
  SpellingsIndex::create_test_trie.

"CxxIME" is used here only to identify the original work.
